<interrogationes unitas="processus">

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I kill a child that uses too much memory?
    <responsum symbolum="processus_exsequi_cum ProcessusOptiones PROCESSUS_ERROR_MEMORIA">memset
      a ProcessusOptiones to zero, set memoria_maxima in bytes and call
      processus_exsequi_cum. The child's footprint (compressed pages
      included, not RSS) is read in the same loop that enforces
      mora_maxima_ms, at most once every 20 ms, so a child that loops
      without printing is caught too. Over the limit it gets SIGKILL and
      the result has successus FALSUM, error PROCESSUS_ERROR_MEMORIA and
      an error_descriptio naming the footprint seen; output captured so
      far is kept. 0 means no limit. processus_incipere (the incremental
      path) takes no options, so it has no memory limit. Always memset
      the options: a field added later would otherwise be read as stack
      garbage.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

</interrogationes>
